# The build context is uploaded to the daemon in full before the first
# instruction runs. Without this file that was 835MB — mostly a local .venv the
# image rebuilds from uv.lock anyway, and a .git directory the image has no use
# for. Slow on every build, and worse: anything here that lands in a layer is
# shipped to a registry.
#
# .env is the one that matters. It holds a live API key, a Fernet vault key and
# the BSP app secret. No COPY in the Dockerfile names it, but a future `COPY . .`
# would, and by then the leak is in a published image layer rather than in a
# diff someone could have reviewed.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.gitleaks.toml
.pre-commit-config.yaml

# Build artefacts and local output, none of which belong in an image.
reports/
evals/artifacts/
infra/.terraform/
infra/*.tfstate*
dashboard/

# Tests are not shipped: the image runs the application, and CI runs the tests
# from a checkout. Copying them in would add the whole tests tree to every pull
# for the benefit of nobody.
tests/

.DS_Store
*.md
!README.md
